<title>USA: CSCE world sugar called to open down 0.05 to 0.10.</title>
<headline>CSCE world sugar called to open down 0.05 to 0.10.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>CSCE world sugar futures were called to open 0.05 to 0.10 cent weaker from Wednesday's close, dealers said, in line with LIFFE.</p>
<p>LIFFE white sugar futures were weakened by midday, with spot December was down $1.40 at $311.50.</p>
<p>Wednesday, CSCE world sugar futures finished barely lower. March ended off 0.02 cent at 10.47 cents a lb after trading from 10.57 to 10.45. The back months settled unchanged to off 0.01.</p>
<p>Volume was estimated at 8,470 lots.</p>
<p>--Suzanne Rostler, New York Commodities Desk 212-859-1640</p>
